      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62b61f8ec938a62475e4cd14|full_name} This is a horrible thing if its intended, especially with the current landscape of storage and computing in general. Its just a useless massive waste of resources, if someone disables something there should be no reason to interact with that at all. Especially since in my experience, if someone disables it they don't want to enable it later down the line during the same instance of the game being open.",
